<title>JAPAN: Zenrin shares rise on Toyota's share purchase.</title>
<headline>Zenrin shares rise on Toyota's share purchase.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of mapmaker Zenrin Co Ltd rose on the Tokyo Stock Exchange on Monday morning on Toyota Motor Corp's acquisition of a five percent stake in Zenrin.</p>
<p>By 0129 GMT, Zenrin shares were up 480 yen at 6,290 yen after being bid only earlier on Monday.  </p>
<p>Toyota said on Friday that it had bought 1.68 million shares, or five percent, of Zenrin in the hope of developing software for better car navigation systems.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition is viewed as a factor which may help expand Zenrin's business,&quot; an official of a medium-sized Japanese brokerage said.</p>
</text>
